ui/base: skip CGWindowListCreateImage when the macOS minimum is >= 15.0.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
The EmberBSD Electron build sets mac_deployment_target = "26.0" for the
host toolchains. The macOS 26 SDK marks CGWindowListCreateImage obsoleted
in macOS 15.0 (hard "unavailable" error) in cocoa/permissions_utils.mm.
The @available(macOS 14.0) ScreenCaptureKit branch always runs there, so
compile the legacy fallback only for lower minimums.

--- a/ui/base/cocoa/permissions_utils.mm	2026-10-28 02:07:51.231962605 +0300
+++ b/ui/base/cocoa/permissions_utils.mm	2026-10-28 02:07:51.234148784 +0300
@@ -94,9 +94,13 @@
                                onScreenWindowsOnly:true
                                  completionHandler:shareable_content_handler];
   } else {
+#if __MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED < 150000
+    // EmberBSD: CGWindowListCreateImage is obsoleted (unavailable) once the
+    // deployment target reaches macOS 15; the SCK branch above always runs.
     base::apple::ScopedCFTypeRef<CGImageRef>(
         CGWindowListCreateImage(CGRectInfinite, kCGWindowListOptionOnScreenOnly,
                                 kCGNullWindowID, kCGWindowImageDefault));
+#endif
   }
 }
 
